    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299-a1">

                <pb facs="0501" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg405"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Boutwell to Mr. Fish.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Treasury Department, Office of the
                            Secretary</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 16, 1872</date>.
                        (Received March 18.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a letter written by Mr.
                    Kenedy, of Brownsville, Texas, to Judge Downey of that place, now in this city.
                    This letter corroborates the statements <pb facs="0502" n="406" xml:id="pg406"/>
                    received from other sources, that American citizens on the line of the Rio
                    Grande are subject to depredations on the other side of the river, and the loss
                    of large numbers of cattle.</p>
                <p>Yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. S. BOUTWELL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
